  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1208 AM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nTemps will be about 3 to 6F cooler on Wednesday than today. Temps \nwill rebound for Thursday and Friday. Dry weather will continue.\n\nFor the weekend, the first in a series of weather systems will move \nacross the region. This system will have the potential to bring some \nshowers to all of the region, with the best chance of seeing some \nhigh elevation snows over Contdvd region. The shower activity \nshould move out of the region by midday Sunday as ridging once \nagain builds over the area. \n\nDry weather should last into Tuesday, but by late in the day another \nlong wave trough amplifies over the western United States, and this \nsystem shows the potential to bring beneficial snow to the mountains \nduring the mid/late week period next week. \\/Hodanish",
